# Feature API Pattern (Auto)

- While building UI/components, always think about API integration from the beginning.
- Each feature should own its API module in its folder:
  - TypeScript projects: `src/features/<feature>/api.ts`
  - JavaScript projects: `src/features/<feature>/api.js`
- Keep all endpoint paths in one central file: `src/api/urls.ts` (or `src/api/urls.js`).
- Use only shared `getData()` and `postData()` from `src/api/httpClient` for API calls.
- Keep UI components free from direct `fetch` calls; call feature API functions instead.
- Keep endpoint paths, payload shapes, and mapping logic inside feature API files.
- Keep API base configuration centralized in config/services, not scattered in components.
- For features without backend ready yet, implement API functions with clear temporary fallback behavior so UI can be wired now and switched later with minimal changes.
- Reuse the same API pattern across all features for consistency and traceability.
